# Explicit allow-list: deny everything, then re-allow only what the image actually needs to
# build and run (see Dockerfile's COPY . . and fly.toml's release_command). A build-context WARN
# ("Build context is 1.3 GB") showed .mtg_json/, pg_dump/, cache/, and debug/ — all local-only
# runtime/dev artifacts, none of them referenced by the Dockerfile — being uploaded on every
# `fly deploy`/`docker build`. Local docker-compose dev is unaffected: cache/ and debug/ are
# bind-mounted over the image at container start (see ../docker-compose.yml), not copied in at
# build time, so excluding them from the build context doesn't remove them from the running
# container. A new local-only directory is excluded by default under this scheme — opt a new
# runtime path in here explicitly instead of remembering to ignore the next one.
*

!app
!app/**
!migrations
!migrations/**
!tasks
!tasks/**
!alembic.ini
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!settings.py
